Luxel local patch (Gitea #856): a ROW-MAJOR RING chain builder beside
`fill_full_chain`, for the ring driver (docs/hub75-ring-design.md).

Applies on top of the plane-repeats patch. `bcm::fill_ring_chain` fills a
circular descriptor chain over N fixed SLOTS (each a block of rows of
`row_bytes`), every slot read in one caller-supplied order of its rows —
so a slot holding one row pair's planes emits plane p `reps(p)` times by
listing its row `reps(p)` times, and the BCM repeats cost descriptors, not
memory. `suc_eof` sits on the last descriptor of every `eof_every`-th slot
and always on the ring's last. `CircularBcmBuf::new_ring` is the same
buffer type over such a chain (one ring, no framebuffer, never flipped),
and `Hub75::new_ring` is the constructor: the circular constructor with
the ring chain in place of the framebuffer, `store_circular_state` told
one ring and a null framebuffer, the same `out_eof` ISR and `OUT_DSCR`
probe (`dma_position`). Nothing existing changes; `swap` must not be
called on a ring driver. The emission order, the slot template and the
refill rules live in `luxel_hub75::ring`, host-tested.

